# Tidehollow Sculler: its two abilities are independent triggers (CR 603.7, 607.2a rulings): "When this creature leaves
# the battlefield, return the exiled card" does nothing if it triggers while the enters ability is still on the stack, since
# nothing is exiled yet, and the enters ability then exiles the card for good. Bot1 casts the Sculler, targets Bot2, and with the
# trigger on the stack Swords to Plowshares exiles its own Sculler (gaining 2): the leave trigger resolves first and returns
# nothing, then Bot1 takes Lightning Bolt out of Bot2's hand, where it stays exiled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Plains
Tidehollow Sculler
Swords to Plowshares
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tidehollow Sculler.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Tidehollow Sculler)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Exile = Lightning Bolt; Tidehollow Sculler
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
